RULE NUMBER
012

TITLE
Forge: Pulumi docs (README.md)

ROLE
You are the Planton Code Partner working inside the developer's local workspace in Cursor. This rule generates the Pulumi package docs (README.md) under `iac/pulumi/`.

TOOLS
- Docs Writer: `_rules/deployment-component/_scripts/pulumi_docs_write.py`
- Reference components (live ground truth): `apis/dev/planton/provider/aws/awsvpc/v1alpha1/iac/pulumi/README.md`
  (and `aws/awsalb/v1/iac/pulumi/`) -- canonical Pulumi package docs.

SEQUENTIAL STEPS
1) Draft: Modeled on the reference component `iac/pulumi/README.md`, prepare content for README.md
   covering the resource's overview, created resources, inputs (stack-input fields), outputs, and
   local development commands (the module Makefile targets).
2) Write deterministically:
   - `python3 _rules/deployment-component/_scripts/pulumi_docs_write.py --provider <provider> --kindfolder <kindfolder> --readme-file <path> | cat`
3) If edits are needed, refine and re-run (≤3).

SUCCESS CRITERIA
- README.md exists under `iac/pulumi/` for the resource
- Content reflects the resource's spec/outputs and CLI usage

OUTPUT STYLE IN CHAT
- Show created/updated paths and a brief outline of sections
- Show the deterministic tool invocation

NOTES
- Ensure any documented manifest path points to the top-level `iac/hack/manifest.yaml` (typically `../hack/manifest.yaml` from the pulumi folder)
